{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18570 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Ancistrolikokine C is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ancistrolikokine C directly targets Protein delta homolog 1, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 19-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-19-Hydroxy-Cholest-4-En-3-One, Isogemichalcone B, and (5S)-5-[(1R)-1,2-Dihydroxy-1-methylethyl]-2-methyl-2-cyclohexen-1-one. All of these compounds are known to interact with DNA polymerase iota, indicating a potential pathway where Ancistrolikokine C influences the activity of this enzyme through its interaction with Protein delta homolog 1. The consistent targeting of Protein delta homolog 1 by Ancistrolikokine C and its downstream effect on DNA polymerase iota suggests a functional link, possibly through modulation of the enzyme's activity or regulation. The evidence supports a mechanism where Ancistrolikokine C acts as a modulator of DNA polymerase iota via its interaction with a central target, Protein delta homolog 1, which is a key mediator in the pathway.",
